Railyard product analytics service
Copyright 2026 Railyard

This service implements the public capture, flags and remote-config wire
protocol of the PostHog SDKs so their unmodified MIT/Apache-2.0 clients can
send to it. Parts are ported from open-source projects:

- PostHog (https://github.com/PostHog/posthog), MIT License (Expat), outside
  the `ee/` directory, commit cbb1e9253027:
  - nodejs/src/common/persons/person-utils.ts: the illegal distinct-id lists
    (src/persons/ids.ts);
  - nodejs/src/common/persons/person-property-utils.ts: the event-to-person
    and campaign property sets (src/persons/properties.ts);
  - nodejs/src/ingestion/common/persons/person-merge-service.ts: identify,
    alias and merge semantics, re-implemented on Postgres
    (src/persons/service.ts);
  - person overrides (merges without rewriting events) and group-type
    numbering semantics (src/persons/overrides.ts, src/groups/groups.ts).
